<title>GERMANY: German Gehe to pull out of production-paper.</title>
<headline>German Gehe to pull out of production-paper.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gehe AG is looking to sell off its generic drugs unit Azupharma, and the buyer will likely be Switzerland's Sandoz AG, an advance copy of an article in Monday's &quot;Handelsblatt&quot; newspaper said.</p>
<p>The move is part of plans by the drugs wholsesaler for a complete withdrawal from medicine production that is expected to net Gehe some 800 million marks of proceeds, the paper added.</p>
<p>It said BASF AG's Knoll AG was already understood to have acquired the French generic production activities owned by Gehe, while the  Stada AG group is thought to have its Aliud Pharma GmbH unit in its sights.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
